 leb.1.t:0 "Joseph Aoun Elected President of Lebanon"
 leb.1.d:0 "General Joseph Aoun is elected President of Lebanon. He breaks a 26-month political vacuum with 99 parliamentary votes. Backed by Washington and Riyadh, the former army chief mandates a strict state monopoly on weapons. Lebanon will now pursue an independent track for regional security negotiations."
 leb.1.a:0 "Good for them"
 leb.2.t:0 "Douma, Lebanon Wins Award as the Most Prominent Touristic Village"
 leb.2.d:0 "Renowned for its breathtaking mountain landscapes and distinct red-brick traditional houses, the village stood out among hundreds of international nominees for its exceptional preservation of cultural heritage. The global accolade recognizes Douma's commitment to economic sustainability, community-based values, and the revival of its historic centuries-old souk. Local officials and the Ministry of Tourism celebrated the achievement as a monumental win that places rural Lebanese hospitality at the forefront of the global travel market. This international honor serves as a beacon of hope for the nation, promising to significantly boost sustainable eco-tourism and cultural exploration in the region."
 leb.2.a:0 "Nice!"
